WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.910
Say these three words:
beef, royal, parliament.

2
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:06.370
They sound English.

3
00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.890
But they came into
English from French.

4
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:12.270
So how did French words
get into everyday English?

5
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:15.270
And how can historians know
about events so long ago,

6
00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:18.110
when nobody alive today was there?

7
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:21.670
In this mission, you'll see a
red rose and a white rose fight

8
00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:25.110
for the throne, until the main
fighting ends at Bosworth,

9
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:26.870
in fourteen eighty-five.

10
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:30.610
You'll learn to question a source,
such as a monk's chronicle:

11
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.430
who made it, when, and why.

12
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:37.590
Your mission: decide how much
ten sixty-six really changed

13
00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:38.650
England.
